    15	
    16	## 1. Execution structure
    17	
    18	**Shot loop (SERIAL):** `src/clifft/svm/svm.cc:299-342`. A plain
    19	`for (uint32_t shot = 0; shot < shots; ++shot)` over one reused
    20	`SchrodingerState`. There is **no per-shot parallelism** — no `omp parallel`,
    21	`std::thread`, or `std::async` wraps the shot loop. Each shot:
    22	`state.reset()` (svm.cc:300-302) → seed next noise gap (svm.cc:304-305,
    23	`draw_next_noise`) → `execute(program, state)` (svm.cc:307) → survivor
    24	bookkeeping (svm.cc:309-341). `sample()`, `sample_k()`, `sample_k_survivors()`
    25	share the identical serial structure.
    26	
    27	**Dispatch loop (per shot):** `src/clifft/svm/svm_kernels.inl:2183`
    28	`execute_internal()`. It is a **computed-goto threaded interpreter**: a
    29	`static const void* dispatch_table[256]` of label addresses
    30	(svm_kernels.inl:2196-2255) indexed by `pc->opcode`; the `DISPATCH()` macro
    31	(svm_kernels.inl:2260-2265) does `++pc; goto *dispatch_table[pc->opcode]`. Each
    32	opcode label calls an `exec_*` handler then `DISPATCH()`. This is a tight,
    33	branch-predictor-friendly loop with per-opcode indirect-branch history.
    34	
    35	**Parallelism that DOES exist — intra-op, gated by rank.** OpenMP `#pragma omp
    36	parallel for` lives *inside* the amplitude sweeps via helpers in
    37	`src/clifft/svm/svm_internal.h:89-267` (`parallel_for`, `parallel_reduce`,
    38	`parallel_flat_loop`, `parallel_stride_loop`, `parallel_3d_stride_loop`). All are
    39	guarded by `if (active_k >= kMinRankForThreads)` where
    40	`kMinRankForThreads = 18` (svm_internal.h:60). **Threads only engage at
    41	active_k ≥ 18** (statevector ≥ 4 MB); below that everything runs single-threaded
    42	to avoid thread-wakeup overhead. State allocation zero-fill is likewise threaded
    43	only at peak_rank ≥ 18 (`svm_state.cc:114`).
    44	
    45	Net: for the vast majority of benchmark circuits (register rank 0-4, coop rank
    46	5-10, most "global" ≤17), **the CPU path is effectively single-threaded**;
    47	throughput is one core running the computed-goto loop `shots` times.
