   209	**Obstacles / friction:**
   210	- `std::complex<double>` is passed to intrinsics via
   211	  `reinterpret_cast<double*>` (re/im interleaved). Complex multiply needs
   212	  shuffle+FMA (`cmul_m512d`); it works but is not free SIMD — real/imag lane
   213	  juggling costs shuffles.
   214	- **Strided permutation gates** (`ARRAY_CNOT/CZ/SWAP` with a high axis) have
   215	  large power-of-two strides → gather-like access, poor cache/TLB locality at
   216	  high rank; SIMD width helps throughput but memory latency dominates.
   217	- The **computed-goto dispatch itself is scalar** and cannot be vectorized —
   218	  for low-rank circuits (§4a) this fixed per-opcode cost, not SIMD width, is the
   219	  limiter.
   220	- OpenMP only helps at active_k ≥ 18; from rank ~11–17 the code is single-core
   221	  bandwidth-limited with SIMD but no thread parallelism (a visible gap).
   222	
   223	---
   224	
   225	## Key takeaways for the perf DB
   226	
   227	1. **Shot loop is serial single-threaded** (svm.cc:299); the only parallelism is
   228	   intra-op OpenMP gated at active_k ≥ 18 (svm_internal.h:60). Most benchmarks
   229	   never cross that threshold → one core.
   230	2. **Cost is bimodal:** frame/Clifford/dormant/classical ops are O(1)
   231	   frame-only; array/expand/active-measurement ops are O(2^active_k). Runtime ≈
   232	   Σ 2^k over the array-touching opcodes.
   233	3. **f64 complex, 16 B/amp, one allocation per call** (huge-paged ≥ 2 MB); no
   234	   hot-path malloc except optional record-keeping.
   235	4. Hotspots shift with rank: **dispatch overhead (rank≤~6) → SIMD phasing/fold
   236	   kernels (rank~7–13) → single-core memory bandwidth (rank~14–17) → multi-core
   237	   bandwidth (rank≥18)**.
   238	5. RNG is a single serial xoshiro256++ stream threaded across all shots — cheap
   239	   but forces the serial shot ordering.
   240	6. Array kernels are already AVX-512/AVX2 hand-tuned with `__restrict` and
   241	   hoisted branches; the practical single-thread ceiling below rank 18 and the
   242	   scalar computed-goto dispatch are the remaining structural limits.

