   242	## 4. The correctness-adapter problem — the smallest shim
   243	
   244	Our check: `run_v2 --circuit C --shots S --seed 1` must produce the same
   245	`passed_shots` + `observable_ones` as `run_gpu --circuit C --shots S --seed 1
   246	--no-postselection`.
   247	
   248	**Permissiveness ranking of the correctness contracts (most → least permissive):**
   249	
   250	1. **KernelForge `test_correctness`** — print `allclose: True` on stdout. Any
   251	   language, any comparison. Exit 0 required. *(Most permissive.)*
   252	2. **Apex `library_test`** — subprocess exit 0 = pass, BUT command must start with
   253	   `pytest`/`python -m pytest`/`python -m unittest`/`python -c`.
   254	3. **Apex `accordo`** — needs `accordo` CLI + two binaries + a float-tolerance GPU
   255	   buffer diff (semantic mismatch with our exact-int check).
   256	4. **Apex `pytorch` / KernelForge SNR path** — needs a torch reference + tensor
   257	   SNR/allclose. *(Most rigid; does not fit us at all.)*
   258	
   259	**The shim (works for BOTH #1 and #2).** A single Python file that runs both
   260	binaries, compares the integer tallies, and speaks both dialects:
   261	
   262	```python
   263	# V2_performance/tools/forge_driver.py  (sketch — NOT created)
   264	import argparse, re, subprocess, sys, os
   265	BASE = "/shared/jmonsalv/quantum/clifft_rl/clifft"
   266	V2   = f"{BASE}/build-v2-nohip/run_v2"
   267	SVM  = f"{BASE}/build-gpu-mlir-mi355x/run_gpu"
   268	
   269	def tally(out):                       # extract passed_shots + observable_ones
   270	    p = re.search(r"passed_shots[:=]\s*(\d+)", out)
   271	    o = re.search(r"observable_ones[:=]\s*(\d+)", out)
   272	    return (p.group(1) if p else None, o.group(1) if o else None)
   273	
   274	def run(cmd):
   275	    return subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True, cwd=BASE).stdout
   276	
   277	ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()
   278	ap.add_argument("--shape", default="")            # "circuit=...,shots=..."
   279	ap.add_argument("--mode", default="")             # smoke/stability/determinism — ignored
   280	ap.add_argument("--bench-mode", action="store_true")
   281	ap.add_argument("--warmup", type=int, default=0); ap.add_argument("--iters", type=int, default=1)
   282	a = ap.parse_args()
   283	kv = dict(p.split("=") for p in a.shape.split(",") if "=" in p)
   284	circ = kv.get("circuit", "tests/fixtures/qv10.stim"); shots = kv.get("shots", "50000")
   285	
   286	if a.bench_mode:
   287	    # rocprofv3 kernel-trace on run_v2 → print median_ms
   288	    #   (parse Avg/Median duration from kt CSV; print "median_ms: <ms>")
   289	    ...
   290	    print(f"median_ms: {kernel_ms:.4f}"); sys.exit(0)
   291	
   292	v2  = tally(run([V2,  "--circuit", circ, "--shots", shots, "--seed", "1"]))
   293	svm = tally(run([SVM, "--circuit", circ, "--shots", shots, "--seed", "1", "--no-postselection"]))
   294	print(f"allclose: {v2 == svm and None not in v2}")
   295	sys.exit(0)                            # exit 0; the loop reads allclose from stdout
   296	```
   297	
   298	For Apex library_test, the same logic collapses into one `--test-cmd`:
   299	`python -c "import subprocess,re,sys; ...; sys.exit(0 if v2==svm else 1)"`.
   300	
   301	(Regex field names above are placeholders — confirm the exact stdout labels
   302	`run_v2`/`run_gpu` print and adjust.)
