   306	## 5. Recommendation
   307	
   308	### Ranking by effort-to-integrate (lowest first)
   309	
   310	1. **KernelForge forge-loop** — LOW/MEDIUM. Correctness (`allclose:`) and bench
   311	   (`median_ms:`) contracts already fit; one driver file + a SLURM wrapper.
   312	   Build routed through the driver (Option A) or a ~40-line direct-`IterationLoop`
   313	   script (Option B). It is a real measurement-driven keep/revert perf loop.
   314	2. **Reusable components only** — LOW. Lift `registers.py`/`pmc.py`/`rocpc`
   315	   classifier into our existing `profile_sweep.sh` workflow; no agentic loop.
   316	   Best if we want profiling insight without an LLM in the loop yet.
   317	3. **Apex optimize-kernel (library_test via `python -c`)** — MEDIUM. Correctness
   318	   fits, but **speedup measurement is bound to Magpie and won't time our HSA
   319	   binary**, gutting the perf signal. Good for grading, weak as an optimizer.
   320	4. **Apex accordo** — HIGH. `accordo` CLI not installed; float-tolerance buffer
   321	   diff mismatches our exact-integer check.
