     1	# V2_performance — clifft MLIR-V2 performance characterization database
     2	
     3	Central database for the V2 (HIP-free/HSA) performance-improvement effort.
     4	Populated by profiling jobs + characterization subagents; consumed by a
     5	parallel Codex + Claude Code planning pass.
     6	
     7	Node: mi350x-es (gfx950 / MI355X / CDNA4). Gold: GPU-SVM (f32) per R3.
     8	
     9	## Layout
    10	
    11	- `tools/`     — tooling availability + how-to (what profilers exist on the
    12	                 compute node, HSA-counter caveats, exact commands used).
    13	- `gpu/`       — per-circuit GPU characterization: kernel time (rocprofv3
    14	                 --kernel-trace), HSA dispatch overhead (--hsa-core-trace),
    15	                 hardware counters (SQ_WAVES/VALU/MFMA/TCC/FETCH/WRITE),
    16	                 rocprof-compute SoL/roofline/occupancy, llvm-objdump
    17	                 VGPR/SGPR/LDS/spill. One subdir/file per circuit; V2 AND SVM.
    18	- `cpu/`       — CPU reference (sample_survivors f64) characterization: wall
    19	                 time, shots/sec, rank/shot scaling, hotspots, memory.
    20	- `raw/`       — raw profiler artifacts (rocprofv3 csv/json, objdump, logs).
    21	- `analysis/`  — cross-circuit synthesis, bottleneck taxonomy, roofline plots.
    22	- `plans/`     — optimization plans (Codex output, Claude output, merged).
    23	
    24	## Key measurement recipes (from ref_amd_profiling_tools + ref_gpu_opt)
    25	
    26	- Clean kernel time:      rocprofv3 --kernel-trace --stats -- <app>
    27	- HSA dispatch overhead:  rocprofv3 --hsa-core-trace -- <app>   (the piece the
    28	                          host-wall baseline conflated; needed for a fair
    29	                          V2-kernel vs SVM-kernel number)
    30	- HW counters:            rocprofv3 -i pmc.txt -- <app>
    31	    pmc: SQ_WAVES SQ_INSTS_VALU SQ_INSTS_MFMA TCC_HIT_sum TCC_MISS_sum FETCH_SIZE WRITE_SIZE
    32	    (MFMA should be ~0 — our compute is 2x2/4x4 butterfly, NOT GEMM. Nonzero = mis-lowering.)
    33	- SoL/roofline/occupancy: rocprof-compute profile -n <name> -- <app>; then analyze -p ...
    34	- Registers/LDS/spill:    llvm-objdump on the .hsaco (occupancy step at VGPR 256;
    35	                          LDS<=80KB => dual-occupancy on CDNA4)
    36	
    37	## Bottleneck classification (KernelForge thresholds)
    38	
    39	- COMPUTE>=60% & BW<40%          -> compute-bound
    40	- BW>=50% & COMPUTE<40%          -> bandwidth-bound
    41	- both<40% & occupancy<40%       -> occupancy-bound
    42	- both<40% & occupancy>=40%      -> latency-bound
    43	- else                           -> balanced
    44	- LDS bank conflicts >= 20%      -> flag lds_bank_conflicts
    45	
    46	## Circuit matrix (BENCHMARKS.md, ranks measured 2026-07-24)
    47	
    48	reg(0-4):  frame_h(r0), circuit_d3(r4)
    49	coop(5-10):qv10(r10), surface_d7_t15(r10), surface_d9_t10(r7), surface_d11_t10(r7)
    50	global(11+):surface_d7_t19(r12), surface_d9_t19(r13), surface_d11_t15(r11),
    51	            surface_d11_t19(r14, KNOWN DIVERGENCE), qv20(r20, over cap)

